   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline><date when="1943-03-27">March 27. 1943</date></dateline><lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4360" type="person">Mr. Friedrich Krause</rs><lb/>
               651 West 177 Str<lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New York City</rs>
               <salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__4360" type="person">Mr. Krause</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>Referring to your <rs ref="#L10606" type="letter">letter of March 26.</rs> I send
               you a list of <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Dr. Tillich</rs>&apos;s 
               manuscripts which still are available. Will you please let <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Dr. Tillich</rs>
            know whether you are interested in all of them and the price of the books.</p>
            <p>The Concept of man in existential philosophy.<lb/>
            July 1939. Journal of Religion. Vol. XIX No 3. <hi rend="underline">5 copies</hi></p>
            <p>Die Idee der Offenbarung.<lb/>
               Theologie und Kirche. 1927 Heft 6 <hi rend="underline">6 copies</hi></p>
            <p>Die Überwindung des Persönlichkeitsideals.<lb/> Internationale Zeitschrift fuer
               Philosophie u. Kultur.<lb/> 1927 <hi rend="underline">3 copies</hi></p>
            <p>Protestantismus als Kritik und Gestaltung.<lb/>
               <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1570">Otto Reichl</rs> Verlag. <rs
                  ref="#tillich_place_id__118" type="place">Darmstadt</rs>. 1929. <hi
                  rend="underline">5 copies</hi></p>
            <p>Der Sozialismus als Krichenfrage.<lb/> Grachtverlag <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__37"
                  type="place">Berlin</rs> 1919 <hi rend="underline">6 copies</hi></p>
            <p>Der Begriff des Uebernatuerlichen, sein dialektischer Charakter und das Prinzip der
               Identitat.<lb/> H. Mdrasch <!-- richtig: Madrasch --><rs ref="#tillich_place_id__245"
                  type="place">Koenigsberg</rs> 1915 <hi rend="underline">6 copies</hi></p>
            <closer>
               <salute>Sincerely yours</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3339" type="person"
                  >Hilde Frankel</rs><lb/>
                  Secretary to <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Prof. Tillich</rs></signed>
            </closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
